D = {
 "Extreme Heat|DMG": "At 100 degrees Fahrenheit or higher, a creature in the heat with no drinkable water makes a Constitution save at the end of each hour. On a failure, it gains one level of exhaustion. The DC is 5 for the first hour and rises by 1 each extra hour. The creature has disadvantage on the save if it wears medium or heavy armor or heavy clothing. Creatures with resistance or immunity to fire damage, or natural adaptation to hot climates, pass the save automatically.",
 "Extreme Heat|XDMG": "At 100 degrees Fahrenheit or higher, a creature in the heat with no drinkable water makes a Constitution save at the end of each hour. On a failure, it gains 1 Exhaustion level. The DC is 5 for the first hour and rises by 1 each extra hour. The creature has Disadvantage on the save if it wears Medium or Heavy armor. Creatures with Resistance or Immunity to Fire damage pass the save automatically.",
 "Falling|XPHB": "A falling creature takes 1d6 Bludgeoning damage per 10 feet fallen when the fall ends, up to 20d6. It lands Prone unless it avoids all damage from the fall. A creature falling into water or another liquid can use its Reaction to try a DC 15 Strength (Athletics) or Dexterity (Acrobatics) check to enter head or feet first. On a success, the fall damage is halved.",
 "Falling into Water|TCE": "A creature falling into water or another liquid can use its reaction to make a DC 15 Strength (Athletics) or Dexterity (Acrobatics) check and hit the surface head or feet first. On a success, the fall damage is halved.",
 "Falling onto a Creature|TCE": "If a creature falls into the space of a second creature and neither is Tiny, the second creature makes a DC 15 Dexterity save. On a failure, the fall damage is split evenly between them. The impacted creature is also knocked prone, unless it is two or more sizes larger than the falling creature.",
 "Fireball Fungus|XDMG": "A fireball fungus is a Small inanimate mushroom with a glowing orange cap. It sheds Bright Light in a 15-foot radius and Dim Light for another 15 feet. It has AC 10, 6 HP, and Immunity to Psychic damage. At 0 Hit Points it explodes as the Fireball spell with save DC 15, centered on it. The blast makes other fireball fungi in the area explode too. For higher levels, add one fungus at levels 11-16 or three fungi at levels 17-20.",
 "Flame Storm|TCE": "Storm clouds with red and orange lightning rain fire. Any creature in the burning rain takes 2d6 fire damage at the start of each of its turns. The droplets ignite flammable objects that are not worn or carried. The noise, smoke, and soot impose disadvantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks and ranged attack rolls. A flame storm usually lasts 2d4 minutes, though the source clouds can last for days and create more storms.",
 "Flaywind|TCE": "Supernatural winds, such as those of Pandemonium, can create a flaywind. It is a violent sandstorm full of grit, rocks, and debris. The area is heavily obscured. A creature exposed to it takes 1d4 slashing damage at the start of each of its turns. Only substantial cover or shelter protects against it. It leaves 4d6 feet of sand or debris behind. A DC 15 Intelligence (Arcana or Nature) or Wisdom (Survival) check spots one 1 minute before it hits. It typically lasts 1d4 x 10 hours.",
 "Frigid Water|DMG": "A creature can stay in frigid water for a number of minutes equal to its Constitution score with no ill effect. Each extra minute, it must succeed on a DC 10 Constitution save or gain one level of exhaustion. Creatures with resistance or immunity to cold damage, or natural adaptation to icy water, pass the save automatically.",
 "Frigid Water|XDMG": "A creature can stay in frigid water for a number of minutes equal to its Constitution score with no ill effect. Each extra minute, it must succeed on a DC 10 Constitution save or gain 1 Exhaustion level. Creatures with Resistance or Immunity to Cold damage, or natural adaptation to icy water, pass the save automatically.",
 "Glittermoss|NF": "Glittermoss is sparkling moss that grows in unstable magic fields, never in direct sunlight. A patch fills a 5-foot square. A creature touching it makes a DC 12 Constitution save. On a failure, it takes 11 (2d10) Radiant damage and has the Blinded condition. While Blinded this way, it sheds Bright Light in a 10-foot radius and Dim Light for another 10 feet. It repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on a success. Any creature that starts its turn in that Bright Light makes a DC 12 Constitution save, taking 11 (2d10) Radiant damage on a failure or half on a success. Any Fire or Necrotic damage destroys a patch instantly.",
 "Green Slime|DMG": "Green slime is acidic and eats flesh, organic matter, and metal. A patch covers a 5-foot square, has blindsight to 30 feet, and drops from walls or ceilings when it senses movement below. A creature aware of the slime avoids it with a DC 10 Dexterity save. Otherwise it cannot be avoided. On contact, a creature takes 5 (1d10) acid damage, and again at the start of each of its turns until the slime is scraped off or destroyed. Against wood or metal, it deals 11 (2d10) acid damage each round. A nonmagical wood or metal tool used to scrape it off is destroyed. Sunlight, any cure for disease, or cold, fire, or radiant damage destroys a patch.",
 "Green Slime|XDMG": "Green slime is acidic and eats flesh, organic matter, and metal. A patch covers a 5-foot square, has Blindsight to 30 feet, and drops from walls or ceilings when it senses movement below. It cannot otherwise move. A creature aware of the slime avoids it with a DC 10 Dexterity save. On contact, a creature takes 5 (1d10) Acid damage, and again at the start of each of its turns until the slime is scraped off (an action) or destroyed. Against wood or metal, it deals 11 (2d10) Acid damage each round. A nonmagical wood or metal item used to scrape it off is destroyed. Direct sunlight or any Cold, Fire, or Radiant damage destroys a patch.",
 "Heavy Precipitation|DMG": "Heavy rain or snowfall makes the whole area lightly obscured. Creatures there have disadvantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on sight. Heavy rain also puts out open flames and gives disadvantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on hearing.",
 "Heavy Precipitation|XDMG": "Heavy rain or snowfall makes the whole area Lightly Obscured. Creatures there have Disadvantage on all Wisdom (Perception) checks. Heavy rain also puts out open flames.",
 "High Altitude|DMG": "Travel at 10,000 feet or higher above sea level is taxing for breathing creatures because the air is thin. Each hour of travel there counts as 2 hours when working out how long the creature can travel. A breathing creature acclimates after 30 days or more at that elevation. It cannot acclimate above 20,000 feet unless it is native to such places.",
 "High Altitude|XDMG": "Travel at 10,000 feet or higher above sea level is taxing for most creatures because the air is thin. Each hour of travel there counts as 2 hours when working out how long the creature can travel. A creature acclimates after 30 days or more at that elevation. It cannot acclimate above 20,000 feet unless it is native to such places.",
 "Improvised Damage|DMG": "Use this table to set damage on the fly. 1d10: burning coals, a falling bookcase, a poison needle. 2d10: lightning strike, a fire pit. 4d10: collapsing tunnel, a vat of acid. 10d10: crushing walls, whirling blades, a lava stream. 18d10: submersion in lava, a crashing flying fortress. 24d10: a vortex on the Plane of Fire, a godlike jaw. By character level, the three damage tiers are: levels 1-4 use 1d10, 2d10, 4d10. Levels 5-10 use 2d10, 4d10, 10d10. Levels 11-16 use 4d10, 10d10, 18d10. Levels 17-20 use 10d10, 18d10, 24d10. They mean setback, dangerous, and deadly. Deadly damage can drop a character to 0 hit points.",
 "Improvised Damage|XDMG": "Use this table to set damage on the fly. 1d10: burning coals, a falling bookcase, a poison needle. 2d10: lightning strike, a firepit. 4d10: collapsing tunnel, a vat of acid. 10d10: crushing walls, whirling blades, lava. 18d10: submersion in lava, a crashing flying fortress. 24d10: a vortex on the Plane of Fire, a godlike jaw. Nuisance and deadly damage by level: levels 1-4 use 5 (1d10) and 11 (2d10). Levels 5-10 use 11 (2d10) and 22 (4d10). Levels 11-16 use 22 (4d10) and 55 (10d10). Levels 17-20 use 55 (10d10) and 99 (18d10). Deadly damage can kill a wounded character.",
 "Inferno|XDMG": "An inferno is a spreading fire of at least four contiguous 10-foot Cubes. Each Cube can be doused with 10 gallons of water. A strong wind blowing for 1 minute adds 1d4 Cubes. Without fuel, it burns out after 1d10 minutes. It deals 22 (4d10) Fire damage to vegetation and objects not worn or carried, at once and at the end of each minute. A creature that enters it for the first time on a turn or starts its turn there takes 22 (4d10) Fire damage and is burning.",
 "Malnutrition|XPHB": "Daily food needs by size: Tiny 1/4 pound, Small 1 pound, Medium 1 pound, Large 4 pounds, Huge 16 pounds, Gargantuan 64 pounds. A creature that eats less than half its need makes a DC 10 Constitution save at day's end or gains 1 Exhaustion level. A creature that eats nothing for 5 days gains 1 Exhaustion level at the end of day 5 and another at the end of each later day. This exhaustion cannot be removed until the creature eats a full day of food.",
 "Necrotic Tempest|TCE": "A storm of dark clouds, skull shapes, and bone-white lightning. Any creature exposed to it, except constructs and undead, makes a DC 13 Constitution save at the end of each minute. On a failure, it takes 3d6 necrotic damage. A creature that dies in the storm rises as a skeleton or zombie, your choice, 1d10 minutes later. The storm lasts 1d4 hours. Afterward, crops wither and wells are undrinkable for 1d4 days.",
 "Planar Effects|XDMG": "Some planes, and regions they touch, affect creatures. Acheronian Bloodlust: gain Temporary Hit Points equal to half your Hit Point maximum whenever you reduce a creature to 0 Hit Points. Arcadian Vitality: immunity to the Frightened and Poisoned conditions. Blessed Beneficence: creatures other than Fiends and Undead gain the Bless spell there. A Long Rest there also grants Lesser Restoration. Gehennan Cruelty: whenever a creature casts a spell, it makes a DC 10 Charisma save or the spell fails and is wasted. Winds of Pandemonium: after each hour, make a DC 10 Wisdom save or gain 1 Exhaustion level, up to 3 from the winds. A Long Rest does not reduce it unless the creature escapes.",
 "Poisonous Gas|XDMG": "Poisonous gas usually fills an enclosed space such as a sewer or tomb, up to ten 10-foot Cubes. It is transparent and smells foul. A source keeps replenishing it, but a strong wind disperses it for 1 minute. A creature that enters it for the first time on a turn or starts its turn there makes a DC 12 Constitution save. It takes 5 (1d10) Poison damage on a failure or half on a success. Creatures in the gas have Disadvantage on Death Saving Throws. Scaling: levels 5-10 deal 11 (2d10) at DC 14. Levels 11-16 deal 22 (4d10) at DC 16. Levels 17-20 deal 55 (10d10) at DC 18.",
 "Quicksand|DMG": "A quicksand pit covers roughly a 10-foot square and is usually 10 feet deep. A creature entering it sinks 1d4+1 feet and is restrained. At the start of each of its turns, it sinks another 1d4 feet. While not fully submerged, it can use its action to escape with a Strength check against DC 10 plus the feet sunk. A fully submerged creature cannot breathe and risks suffocation. A creature can use its action to pull another creature within reach out with a Strength check against DC 5 plus the feet that creature has sunk.",
 "Quicksand Pit|XDMG": "A quicksand pit is 10 feet deep and covers a 10-foot square. A creature entering it sinks 1d4 + 1 feet and has the Restrained condition. At the start of each of its turns, it sinks another 1d4 feet. While not fully submerged, it can take an action to escape with a Strength (Athletics) check against DC 10 plus feet sunk. A fully submerged creature has Cover and the Blinded condition and risks suffocation. Pulling another creature out takes an action and a Strength (Athletics) check against DC 5 plus its feet sunk. Scaling: levels 5-10 use 15 feet deep, 1d6 sinking. Levels 11-16 use 20 feet, 1d8. Levels 17-20 use 30 feet, 1d10.",
 "Razorvine|DMG": "Razorvine grows in tangles and hedges and clings to walls like ivy. A wall or hedge of it, 10 feet high, 10 feet wide, and 5 feet thick, has AC 11, 25 hit points, and immunity to bludgeoning, piercing, and psychic damage. A creature in direct contact with it for the first time on a turn must succeed on a DC 10 Dexterity save or take 5 (1d10) slashing damage.",
 "Razorvine|XDMG": "Razorvine grows in tangles and hedges and clings to walls like ivy. A wall or hedge of it, 10 feet high, 10 feet wide, and 5 feet thick, has AC 11, 25 HP, and Immunity to Bludgeoning, Piercing, and Psychic damage. A creature in contact with it for the first time on a turn must succeed on a DC 10 Dexterity save or take 5 (1d10) Slashing damage.",
 "River Styx|XDMG": "The River Styx runs through the Lower Planes and wipes minds and memories. Certain Fiends are immune. Any other creature that drinks from it, enters it, or starts its turn in it makes a DC 20 Intelligence save. On a failure, it takes 19 (3d12) Psychic damage and cannot cast spells or take the Magic action for 30 days. An affected creature suffers no further effects from drinking or swimming. Only Greater Restoration, Heal, or Wish ends the effect. After 30 days it becomes permanent and the creature loses all memories. Then only Wish or divine intervention can undo it. Styx water turns harmless after 24 hours. Arcanaloths, night hags, and similar creatures might know rituals to extend it.",
 "Rockslide|XDMG": "Every creature in a rockslide's path makes a DC 15 Dexterity save. On a failure, it takes 11 (2d10) Bludgeoning damage, has the Prone condition, and moves with the slide. On a success, it takes half damage only. When the slide stops, its space is Difficult Terrain and Prone creatures there are buried, Restrained, and have Cover. As an action, a buried creature can try a DC 15 Strength (Athletics) check. On a success, it is Prone atop the pile. On a failure, it gains 1 Exhaustion level. A creature that is neither Incapacitated nor Restrained can spend 1 minute freeing a buried creature. Scaling: 22 (4d10) at levels 5-10, 55 (10d10) at 11-16, 99 (18d10) at 17-20.",
 "Rot Grub|VGM": "Rot grubs are finger-sized maggots that feed on living and dead creatures and infest corpses and rot. Once inside a body, they burrow toward vital parts. Fire is the main weapon against them, and magic that neutralizes poison can stop them. A swarm uses the swarm of rot grubs stat block. A single grub has no stat block. A creature touching one must succeed on a DC 10 Constitution save or be poisoned as it burrows in. The poisoned creature takes 3 (1d6) poison damage at the end of each of its turns. Whenever it takes fire damage, it can repeat the save, ending the effect on a success. If it ends its turn at 0 hit points, it dies.",
 "Russet Mold|VGM": "Russet mold grows in dark, warm, wet places. A DC 15 Intelligence (Nature) or Wisdom (Survival) check identifies it. Within 5 feet, a creature makes a DC 13 Constitution save. On a failure, it is poisoned and takes 7 (2d6) poison damage at the start of each of its turns. It repeats the save each turn's end, ending the effect on a success. Its Beast, Giant, or Humanoid victims sprout vegepygmies after 24 hours: 1 from Small, 2 Medium, 4 Large, 8 Huge, 16 Gargantuan. Only acid, necrotic, or radiant damage hurts it, clearing 1 square foot per damage. A pound of salt, a gallon of alcohol, or cure disease magic clears 10 feet square. Sunlight kills it.",
 "Shadowbark|NF": "Under the shadow of Netheril's flying cities, trees can grow shadowbark, a purple-black moss-like coating that looks like a bruise. A creature that enters a space within 5 feet of it for the first time on a turn or starts its turn there makes a DC 12 Constitution save. On a failure, it takes 5 (1d10) Necrotic damage and cannot regain Hit Points until the start of its next turn. On a success, it takes half damage only. Any Radiant damage destroys it instantly. Scaling: levels 5-10 deal 11 (2d10) at DC 14. Levels 11-16 deal 22 (4d10) at DC 16. Levels 17-20 deal 55 (10d10) at DC 18.",
 "Slippery Ice|DMG": "Slippery ice is difficult terrain. A creature moving onto it for the first time on a turn must succeed on a DC 10 Dexterity (Acrobatics) check or fall prone.",
 "Slippery Ice|XDMG": "Slippery ice is Difficult Terrain. A creature that moves onto it for the first time on a turn or starts its turn there must succeed on a DC 10 Dexterity save or have the Prone condition.",
 "Strong Wind|DMG": "Strong wind gives disadvantage on ranged weapon attack rolls and on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on hearing. It puts out open flames, disperses fog, and makes nonmagical flight nearly impossible. A flying creature must land at the end of its turn or fall. In a desert, strong wind can raise a sandstorm that gives disadvantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on sight.",
 "Strong Wind|XDMG": "Strong wind gives Disadvantage on ranged weapon attack rolls. It puts out open flames and disperses fog. A flying creature must land at the end of its turn or fall. In a desert, it can raise a sandstorm that gives Disadvantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks.",
 "Suffocation|XPHB": "A creature can hold its breath for 1 minute plus its Constitution modifier in minutes, with a minimum of 30 seconds. After that, or when it is choking, it gains 1 Exhaustion level at the end of each of its turns. When it can breathe again, it removes all Exhaustion levels gained from suffocating.",
 "Thin Ice|DMG": "Thin ice holds 3d10 x 10 pounds per 10-foot square. If the total weight on an area exceeds that, the ice there breaks and all creatures on it fall through.",
 "Thin Ice|XDMG": "Thin ice holds 3d10 x 10 pounds per 10-foot square. If the total weight on an area exceeds that, the ice there breaks and all creatures on it fall through. Frigid water lies below.",
 "Thrym's Howl|TCE": "A blizzard that drives a wall of wind and snow like a glacier. It brings extreme cold. The area is heavily obscured, and ranged attack rolls and Wisdom (Perception) checks in it have disadvantage. A creature exposed at the start of its turn takes 2d6 cold damage and cannot regain hit points until it spends at least 1 hour in a warm place. A creature that dies in the storm freezes solid. Creatures immune to cold damage are immune to the storm and see normally in it. It typically lasts 2d10 hours.",
 "Vicious Vine|XDMG": "Magic animates vicious vines. Each has AC 11, 16 HP, and Immunity to Bludgeoning, Piercing, and Psychic damage. A creature entering a space within 5 feet for the first time on a turn or starting its turn there must succeed on a DC 12 Dexterity save or have the Grappled condition (escape DC 12). While Grappled, it takes 5 (1d10) Necrotic damage at the start of each of its turns. A vine grapples one creature at a time. As an Influence action, a character with Speak with Plants can pass a DC 10 Charisma (Persuasion) check to free the victim. Scaling, damage and DC: levels 5-10 11 (2d10), 14. Levels 11-16 22 (4d10), 16. Levels 17-20 55 (10d10), 18.",
 "Webs|DMG": "Giant spiders weave sticky webs across passages and pit bottoms. Webbed areas are difficult terrain. A creature entering one for the first time on a turn or starting its turn there must succeed on a DC 12 Dexterity save or be restrained. A restrained creature can use its action to escape with a DC 12 Strength (Athletics) or Dexterity (Acrobatics) check. Each 10-foot cube of webs has AC 10, 15 hit points, vulnerability to fire, and immunity to bludgeoning, piercing, and psychic damage.",
 "Webs|XDMG": "Giant spiders weave sticky webs across passages and pit bottoms. Webbed areas are Difficult Terrain. A creature entering one for the first time on a turn or starting its turn there must succeed on a DC 12 Dexterity save or have the Restrained condition. As an action, a Restrained creature can escape with a DC 12 Strength (Athletics) or Dexterity (Acrobatics) check. Each 10-foot Cube of webs has AC 10, 15 HP, Vulnerability to Fire damage, and Immunity to Piercing, Poison, and Psychic damage.",
 "Wild Magic Zone|XDMG": "A magical disaster or power surge can unravel magic in an area, usually no more than 300 feet across. Magic behaves unpredictably there. Whenever a creature expends a spell slot to cast a spell in the zone, roll 1d20. On a 20, roll on the Wild Magic Surge table in the Player's Handbook for a magical effect.",
 "Wildstorm|NF": "A wildstorm is a tornado of unstable magic filling a 10-foot Cube, with Speed 50 feet. Each round on Initiative count 0 (losing ties), it moves to the nearest creature. It lasts 1d4 minutes. A creature entering it or starting its turn there rolls a random effect. 1-2: 2 (1d4) Fire damage, burning. 3-6: DC 12 Dexterity save, 5 (1d10) Force damage, half on success. 7-10: DC 12 Constitution save or Poisoned 1 minute, or 5 (2d4) Poison damage if already Poisoned. 11-13: DC 12 Wisdom save, 5 (1d10) Psychic damage, half on success, plus 10-foot telepathy for 1 minute. 14-17: Vulnerability to Fire, Force, Poison, Psychic, 1 minute. 18-19: +2 AC, 1 minute. 20: Invisible, 1 minute.",
 "Witchbriars|NF": "Low Netherese witches enchant thorn patches called witchbriars. They look like an ordinary thorny hedge. A patch fills a 10-foot Cube and has AC 11, 30 HP, and Immunity to Bludgeoning, Piercing, and Psychic damage. When a creature casts a spell using a spell slot within 10 feet, vines reach for it. It must succeed on a DC 14 Strength save or have the Grappled condition (escape DC 14). Druids pass automatically. While Grappled this way, it is Restrained and takes 11 (2d10) Piercing damage at the start of each of its turns. One patch can grapple up to four creatures. Any Fire damage destroys a patch instantly.",
 "Yellow Mold|DMG": "Yellow mold grows in dark places, one patch to a 5-foot square. If touched, it ejects spores in a 10-foot cube from the mold. Creatures in the area must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution save or take 11 (2d10) poison damage and be poisoned for 1 minute. While poisoned, a creature takes 5 (1d10) poison damage at the start of each of its turns. It repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on a success. Sunlight or any fire damage instantly destroys a patch.",
 "Yellow Mold|XDMG": "Yellow mold grows in dark places, one patch to a 5-foot square. If touched, it ejects spores in a 10-foot Cube. Creatures in the area must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution save or take 11 (2d10) Poison damage and have the Poisoned condition for 1 minute. While Poisoned, a creature takes 5 (1d10) Poison damage at the start of each of its turns. It repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on a success. Direct sunlight or any Fire damage destroys a patch.",
 "Hailstorm|FRAIF": "A hailstorm bombards travelers with falling ice. Exposed creatures make a Constitution save at the end of each hour or gain 1 Exhaustion level. The DC is 5 for the first hour and rises by 1 for each additional hour. Creatures wearing Medium or Heavy armor have Advantage on the save.",
 "Howling Wind|FRAIF": "The winds of Icewind Dale can grow so loud that hearing is impossible. Creatures outdoors in howling winds have the Deafened condition.",
 "Lightning Strikes|FRAIF": "When part of the Calim Desert has both strong wind and heavy precipitation, there is a 25 percent chance a lightning storm forms. It lasts 1 hour. After each minute in the area, a creature rolls 1d6. On a 1, lightning strikes it, and it makes a DC 15 Dexterity save, taking 3d10 Lightning damage on a failure or half on a success. A creature that succeeds on a DC 10 Intelligence (Nature) or Wisdom (Survival) check predicts a lightning storm 1d4 hours before it forms nearby.",
 "Magical Mirage|FRAIF": "Ambient magic creates magical mirages. One seems real, with fitting sounds and smells, but it cannot deal damage or cause conditions. Things pass through it, so touching it reveals the illusion. A mirage might show an oasis whose pond is only a sandy pit. Examples include lively oases and pristine ancient temples. As a Study action, a creature can inspect it with a DC 15 Intelligence (Investigation) check. On a success, the mirage becomes faint to that creature.",
 "Nonmagical Mirage|FRAIF": "Nonmagical mirages range from simple tricks, such as shimmering water a few miles away, to complex images of huge monsters crossing the horizon. They make no sound and move out of reach if approached. Examples include distant shimmering water, far-off dragons, and floating lights.",
 "Psionic Field|FRAIF": "Resonances from the Underdark touch those who go too deep. Each creature in a psionic field makes an Intelligence save at the end of each hour or gains 1 Exhaustion level. The DC is 5 for the first hour and rises by 1 for each additional hour. A creature that starts and finishes a Long Rest in the field has disturbing dreams and hallucinations. It then has the Frightened condition for 1d10 minutes, afraid of the first creature it saw after the rest.",
 "Sinkhole|FRAIF": "A sinkhole is a cavity in hard earth with sand filling its top half. When a creature steps on the sand, the ground collapses and strands it below. As a Search action, a creature can spot one with a DC 15 Wisdom (Perception) check, and then it can usually be avoided. A creature that walks onto it must succeed on a DC 10 Dexterity check or fall 10 feet. A creature without a Climb Speed climbs out with a DC 15 Strength (Athletics) check. Scaling by depth: levels 5-10 use 30 feet, levels 11-16 use 60 feet, levels 17-20 use 120 feet.",
 "Zlanic Chardalyn|FRAIF": "When Zlan focuses on chardalyn, it becomes charged with negative energy and carries Zlan's will. A creature touching it makes a DC 12 Charisma save. On a failure, the DM picks one effect, which ends 1 minute after the creature stops touching the stone. Option one: the Frightened condition. Option two: the Stunned condition. Option three: Charmed by Zlan, regarding anyone who would separate it from the chardalyn as an enemy.",
}
